# Production build configuration. COMMITTED ON PURPOSE.
#
# Vite inlines VITE_* variables at build time, so this value ends up in the
# shipped bundle and is public by definition. It is a service address, not a
# secret; nothing here is sensitive.
#
# WHY LOCALHOST, IN A DEPLOYED BUNDLE, ON PURPOSE THIS TIME
# ---------------------------------------------------------
# iMATCH is an individual tool. The Vercel deployment is the shell -- the
# marketing site and the workspace UI -- and the recognition engine runs on
# the owner's own machine, where the data lives. The deployed page therefore
# calls the API at localhost: it works exactly where the backend is running
# (the owner's laptop, `backend` entry in .claude/launch.json) and nowhere
# else, which is the point. Browsers permit https pages to call
# http://localhost -- loopback is exempt from mixed-content blocking.
#
# An earlier revision pinned https://nexgen-imatch-api.onrender.com here, when
# the plan was split cloud hosting on free tiers. That backend is retired; the
# comment in the git history of this file records why the dashboard-variable
# approach failed before it.
#
# Keep this in step with vercel.json's Content-Security-Policy connect-src and
# the backend's NEXGEN_CORS_ORIGINS (which must list the Vercel origin), or
# every call from the deployed page fails.
VITE_IMATCH_API_BASE=http://localhost:8443
